@57[end]. As the finite has not anything of the Divine in it...

@TCR 27. (Space and time) cause all things in the natural world to be finite... These finite it.

@29[3]. (Thus) spaces and times finite each and all things in both worlds; and therefore men are finite, not only as to their bodies, but also as to their souls.

@--. (Thus) God is infinite, that is, not finite, because He... has finited all things; and He finited them by means of His Sun... There and thence is the first of finiteness. @33, Explained.

@33. That every created thing is finite; and the infinite is in finites as in receptacles... General article. @CanonsNC 6. God 3. 8.

@--[end]. God first finited His infinity by means of substances emitted from Himself, from which existed His proximate encompassing sphere, which constitutes the Sun... Thus, by means of degrees, He finited the world more and more.

@470[3]. The spirit of man is also created from finite things, (which are) spiritual substances.

@SE 3484. That I might not be kept in... very finite things... there was given me a notion of forms which transcend geometrical forms... Still, all these forms are finite...

@DMin 4609[2]. Time and space are what finite human ideas...

@--. Man can have a finite idea of the Lord's Divine Human, from...

@AE 629[15]. Quantity and quality are properties of the finite; for they determine the finite, and terminate it.

@1131[4]. How the finite receives the infinite, may be illustrated by...

@DLove 4[2]. How the proceeding Divine can be in... finites. Explained.

Fir.; Abies.

