@--[end]. Moreover, "fire" = celestial love, and thence zeal for truth; and in the opposite sense, infernal love, and thence zeal for falsity.

@636. "Shall be tormented with fire and brimstone..." (Revelation 14:10) = the love of self and the love of the world and the cupidities therefrom... @AE 888.

@648. "Having Power over fire" (Revelation 14:18) = ... that the Angels guard the Divine love in themselves. @AE 916.

@655[8]. There appeared as it were fire from Heaven which consumed them; but the fire from Heaven was an appearance of their anger from hatred... @714[end].

@659. "Mingled with fire" (Revelation 15:2) = religion and worship, but no good of life... "Fire," here, = the love of evil, and from it evil of life. ( = the good of love. @AE 931.)

@674. The fire of the altar of burnt-offering = celestial love; and the fire of the altar of incense, spiritual love. References.

@763[2]. Hatred against the Lord, and against all things of Heaven and the Church, is meant by the fire in Hell.

@766. "She shall be utterly burnt with fire" (Revelation 18:8) = that they will be hatreds against the Lord, and against His Heaven and Church.

@--[2]. Infernal fire is hatred, because the love of self hates...

@--[end]. To be burned with fire is the penalty of the profanation of what is holy.

@835. "The lake of fire burning with brimstone" (Revelation 19:20) = the Hell where are they who are in the loves of this falsity, and at the same time in the cupidities of evil. @864. @893.

@863. "Fire came down from God out of Heaven and consumed them" (Revelation 20:9) = that they perished by the concupiscences of infernal love. Explained.

